  "id": "DrugBank_DB00997 - MONDO_18171",
  "verbalization": "Doxorubicin is implicated in the treatment of malignant germ cell tumors of the ovary through a chain of indications that connect it to alternative malignancies, which in turn are linked to the target condition. The evidence suggests that Doxorubicin may be used in the management of ovarian clear cell adenocarcinoma and mucinous adenocarcinoma, both of which are indicated to interact with altretamine and tretamine, which are themselves linked to the malignant germ cell tumor of the ovary. While the exact mechanism of action remains unclear, the presence of these indirect pathways implies a potential role for Doxorubicin in the treatment of this tumor, possibly through its antitumor effects that are mediated by these secondary malignancies. The integration of these indications highlights a possible pathway where Doxorubicin may exert its therapeutic effect via a complex network of related cancers, underscoring the importance of considering broader disease contexts in drug repurposing efforts.",
